// ============================================================================
//  _export_eventhouse.kql — AUTHORING-SIDE. Export the Eventhouse historical
//  data to parquet so it can be bundled and re-ingested in the new workspace.
//
//  Run these against the SOURCE Eventhouse (pi-realtime-db). Each writes parquet
//  to a storage location you control (SAS URL) or to the lakehouse OneLake path.
//  Then place the files under the solution's  data/eventhouse/.
//
//  Full PiEvents history is the chat agent's trend source, so export it in full.
//  The other tables are small.
// ============================================================================

// PiEvents (full history) -> parquet
.export compressed to parquet (
    h@"https://<youraccount>.blob.core.windows.net/pmbundle/PiEvents;<SAS>"
) with (sizeLimit=1073741824, namePrefix="PiEvents", includeHeaders="firstFile")
<| PiEvents

// Curated / small operational tables (export each the same way)
.export compressed to parquet ( h@"https://<youraccount>.blob.core.windows.net/pmbundle/AimmWorkRequests;<SAS>" ) with (namePrefix="AimmWorkRequests") <| AimmWorkRequests
.export compressed to parquet ( h@"https://<youraccount>.blob.core.windows.net/pmbundle/AimmEntityHierarchy;<SAS>" ) with (namePrefix="AimmEntityHierarchy") <| AimmEntityHierarchy
.export compressed to parquet ( h@"https://<youraccount>.blob.core.windows.net/pmbundle/PCIOutages;<SAS>" ) with (namePrefix="PCIOutages") <| PCIOutages
.export compressed to parquet ( h@"https://<youraccount>.blob.core.windows.net/pmbundle/PITagMetadata;<SAS>" ) with (namePrefix="PITagMetadata") <| PITagMetadata
.export compressed to parquet ( h@"https://<youraccount>.blob.core.windows.net/pmbundle/SmartSignalIncidents;<SAS>" ) with (namePrefix="SmartSignalIncidents") <| SmartSignalIncidents

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  Re-ingest in the NEW Eventhouse (after schema.kql created the tables):
//    .ingest into table PiEvents (h'<url-to-parquet>;<SAS>') with (format='parquet')
//  Repeat per table. For OneLake-hosted parquet, use the onelake path + token.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
